// Airline Management System


// Functional Requirements (FR)
1. User should be able to search flights using source, destination, and travel date.
2. User should be able to view flight details.
3. User should be able to view available seats for a flight.
4. User should be able to book a seat.
5. System should generate a Booking ID after successful booking.
6. User should be able to make payment.
7. System should confirm booking after successful payment.
8. System should mark the selected seat as BOOKED.
9. User should be able to cancel a booking.
10. System should release the seat after cancellation.
11. User should be able to view booking details.


// Non Functional Requirements (NFR)
1. Design should be modular.
2. Design should follow SOLID principles.
3. Low coupling and high cohesion.
4. Design should be scalable.
5. Design should be maintainable and testable.
6. Design should support adding new payment methods.
7. Design should support adding new notification channels.


Entities
1. Airline
2. Flight
3. Seat
4. User
5. Booking
6. Payment
7. BookingService
8. NotificationService
9. SeatStatus (enum)
10. BookingStatus (enum)
11. PaymentStatus (enum)
